<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    What a household keeps in its house besides its beds (comfort lane): a table to eat at, and the furnishings
    of its age. HouseFurnishing places them on a house's table spot (t) and furnishing spot (f) once the town
    knows how to make them; Dwellings.xml says which rungs keep which spots.

    The table is RimWorld's (a dining table a colonist carries a meal to, Toils_Ingest's chew spot, recalled),
    1x1 here and with no chair: the seat is folded into it. It comes with the longhouse's research, Shelter:
    the first house built for a settled household is the first with a table in it, and nobody misses a table
    who has never had one (Thoughts_Comfort.xml).

    The furnishings are this port's own and stand for everything RimWorld's colonists make a room impressive
    with that this port does not model one by one: floors, quality furniture, art on the walls. One rung per
    era from Agrarian, each worth more and better to look at than the last, and each replaces the one before it
    in place (GenConstruct.ReplaceTag "Furnishing"). Beauty, MarketValue, WorkToBuild and the wood they cost
    are SimWorld's figures, not sourced; RoomStatsTests pins that each era's house makes a better room than
    the one before, never the numbers. Wood for all of them, because a builder can always fell a tree for a
    blueprint that wants logs: a furnishing the town cannot pay for in the material it has would be a comfort
    that never arrives.
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>DiningTable</defName>
    <label>table</label>
    <description>A table and somewhere to sit at it. A meal is better eaten at one.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Building</thingClass>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>30</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.4</fillPercent>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>500</WorkToBuild>
      <Flammability>1</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <stuffCategories>
      <li>Woody</li>
      <li>Stony</li>
      <li>Metallic</li>
    </stuffCategories>
    <costStuffCount>20</costStuffCount>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Shelter</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Blueprint_DiningTable</defName>
    <label>table (blueprint)</label>
    <category>Blueprint</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Blueprint</thingClass>
    <passability>Standable</passability>
    <entityToBuild>DiningTable</entityToBuild>
  </ThingDef>

